mod lexical_reject_escape_newline;

// A backslash right before a line's end, in a string and in a character
// literal. The backslash is an invalid escape, reported at the literal's
// opening quote. The escape took the line's end with it without counting the
// line, so every later diagnostic in the file came out one line early. Each
// later '$' below is reported on its own line, at its own column: the line
// numbers and columns are the assertion here, and are written by hand.
//
// lexical_reject_escape_newline_crlf is the same file with CRLF line ends,
// which were always counted. This file is kept LF byte for byte
// (.gitattributes). A multi-line string's backslash before a line's end is
// not an escape but a line join; lexical_mlstring runs it.
//
// The literals cut by a line's end cannot carry their annotations, so these
// sit on the line after, pointing back two lines.

fn afterString(a i32) i32 {
  imm s = "x\
y";
  //~^^ ErrorBadTok:11 "Invalid escape sequence: a backslash at the end of a line"
  a $ a;               //~ ErrorBadTok:5 "Bad character '$' starting unknown token"
                       //~^ ErrorNoSemi:4 follow-on
  a;
}

// The escape's line end is followed by the literal's closing quote
fn afterChar(a i32) i32 {
  imm c = '\
';
  //~^^ ErrorBadTok:11 "Invalid escape sequence: a backslash at the end of a line"
  a $ a;               //~ ErrorBadTok:5 "Bad character '$' starting unknown token"
                       //~^ ErrorNoSemi:4 follow-on
  a;
}

// Something other than the closing quote follows the line end, so the literal
// is too long as well. That is said at its opening quote, on the line the
// literal begins, though the line after it has been counted by then.
fn afterLongChar(a i32) i32 {
  imm c = '\
x';
  //~^^ ErrorBadTok:11 "Invalid escape sequence: a backslash at the end of a line"
  //~^^^ ErrorBadTok:11 "Invalid lifetime or too-long character literal" follow-on
  a $ a;               //~ ErrorBadTok:5 "Bad character '$' starting unknown token"
                       //~^ ErrorNoSemi:4 follow-on
  a;
}
